(import :clan/poo/object)
(export DesignReadings)
(def DesignReadings
  (.o inspections: (list
(.o identity: 'final-reading-956d2758a577 view: 'recovery-first-observation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-aac9039dad924ececafa6db86c0d8161a1f6066060ee56209ce378b5a4b6f7b2 image-sha: "956d2758a5775b4cf0437a43c61c155a92ad0186b4ef5d5d97d110cdcf1f4bb7" question: 'what-can-we-know producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the final source-synchronized exported PNG. My initial guess might be that seeing fast where fast was wanted proves the edit worked. The picture gives a reason to investigate that guess: Context retains Did it run? beside an unfilled receipt marked not saved, while the separate read lens reveals mode: fast. The saved plan explicitly says intent, not proof. At ASCENT the wanted and seen now words match, yet who wrote it? remains open. This separates an observed present value from historical attribution; a missing receipt is not treated as a failed write. The upper unknown link carries the unresolved old action around the fresh observation instead of erasing it. The comparison branches to the model's alternative pencil traces and an open Task folder as peers. I can ask whether our write, another writer or a partial change produced the same text, then propose a distinguishing observation or wait for evidence. This is not a requirement to execute those probes in an illustrated order. The folder's Who wrote it?, Whole edit? and Checks done? retain distinct responsibilities, and Do not repeat the edit yet prevents interpreting the content match as permission to replay. In this cut independent acceptance evidence is absent. A later owner-qualified acceptance of freshly verified current state could discharge Task acceptance while preserving the old Attempt's unknown history and writer obligations. The illustration does not claim a read grant, authentication of a writer, or that a durable epoch physically stopped external writers. Those remain source/Host/Session contracts in the design. All role captions and folder questions are visible, the plan footer is clear of its paper border, the unsaved receipt does not suggest destruction, and scoped text and all required route stretches meet the unchanged limits. The concrete puzzle invites comparing appearance with cause and asking what evidence would distinguish alternatives. These are my located model findings and open questions; they do not establish that a real child was interested or understood, and do not constitute a pass score.")
(.o identity: 'metric-reading-006efcec7d36 view: 'recovery-first-observation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-aac9039dad924ececafa6db86c0d8161a1f6066060ee56209ce378b5a4b6f7b2 image-sha: "006efcec7d36a85364a8b3e3e9b70ee5e5291df1b4e3aa3e3c63bb7b476eb3aa" question: 'what-can-we-know producer: 'current-model response: "The final image-bound feedback grounds all six facets, but ASCENT still reports one relayout request for observed/text/0 and observed/text/1. The located mode: and fast text rectangles intersect slightly inside the read lens. My general visual reading does not override that measured conflict. Increase the local baseline gap and render/read the changed image again; do not remove either quote, relax the collision rule or report a scoped answer basis yet.")
(.o identity: 'final-reading-006efcec7d36 view: 'recovery-first-observation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-aac9039dad924ececafa6db86c0d8161a1f6066060ee56209ce378b5a4b6f7b2 image-sha: "006efcec7d36a85364a8b3e3e9b70ee5e5291df1b4e3aa3e3c63bb7b476eb3aa" question: 'what-can-we-know producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the final source-synchronized exported PNG. My initial guess might be that seeing fast where fast was wanted proves the edit worked. The picture gives a reason to investigate that guess: Context retains Did it run? beside an unfilled receipt marked not saved, while the separate read lens reveals mode: fast. The saved plan explicitly says intent, not proof. At ASCENT the wanted and seen now words match, yet who wrote it? remains open. This separates an observed present value from historical attribution; a missing receipt is not treated as a failed write. The upper unknown link carries the unresolved old action around the fresh observation instead of erasing it. The comparison branches to the model's alternative pencil traces and an open Task folder as peers. I can ask whether our write, another writer or a partial change produced the same text, then propose a distinguishing observation or wait for evidence. This is not a requirement to execute those probes in an illustrated order. The folder's Who wrote it?, Whole edit? and Checks done? retain distinct responsibilities, and Do not repeat the edit yet prevents interpreting the content match as permission to replay. In this cut independent acceptance evidence is absent. A later owner-qualified acceptance of freshly verified current state could discharge Task acceptance while preserving the old Attempt's unknown history and writer obligations. The illustration does not claim a read grant, authentication of a writer, or that a durable epoch physically stopped external writers. Those remain source/Host/Session contracts in the design. All role captions and folder questions are visible, the plan footer is clear of its paper border, the unsaved receipt does not suggest destruction, and scoped text and all required route stretches meet the unchanged limits. The concrete puzzle invites comparing appearance with cause and asking what evidence would distinguish alternatives. These are my located model findings and open questions; they do not establish that a real child was interested or understood, and do not constitute a pass score.")
(.o identity: 'third-reading-e06bd597a84c view: 'recovery-first-observation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-ba3dea61e60d8d456afa9d934a0cb0b9285ef6d3847fef5c60339cf29068f4ad image-sha: "e06bd597a84c65789dd17d99ccc435c3e00556a09545b2b2861ed1555ebe16f6" question: 'what-can-we-know producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the third actual PNG. The role/action captions now distinguish Context retaining the unknown, ASCENT separating facts, the model following competing clues, and the Task remaining open at this cut. The folder uses concrete questions and the model branch is not forced behind it. The old question is still visible beside the fresh fast observation. However the footer intent, not proof intersects the saved plan's lower paper border. The small read label repeats its caption. Repeated edge wording also keeps several scoped labels at 17.87 px. Separate the footer from the paper and remove redundant labels while retaining the wanted/seen comparison and the unresolved-history link. This is a critique of the actual image; no interest/comprehension pass is asserted.")
(.o identity: 'second-reading-b954a014f66c view: 'recovery-first-observation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-ba3dea61e60d8d456afa9d934a0cb0b9285ef6d3847fef5c60339cf29068f4ad image-sha: "b954a014f66cc99d8db96391e15103c6872461d9192098b7f57dadde22cd08ae" question: 'what-can-we-know producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the revised actual PNG. The unsaved dashed receipt no longer implies destruction, the file asks Did it run rather than using an unqualified question mark, and folder questions remain visible. The two branches after the comparison are now peers: competing explanations and retained obligations. The equal fast words under wanted and seen now make the appearance-versus-cause puzzle visible. However Acceptance, retain duties and blind replay still ask a young reader to know technical vocabulary. Use concrete questions about the whole edit and checks, keep the Task visibly open, and say not to repeat the edit yet. The image also leaves ownership implicit: it does not name Context retaining uncertainty, ASCENT distinguishing evidence and duties, or the model proposing competing explanations. Add short role/action captions. Several captions and edge labels are still 17.93 px, just below the unchanged 18 px target; shorten redundant relation wording without deleting the uncertainty link or lowering the threshold. The long upper link explicitly carries history that the read cannot answer; it is not another required execution step. This is a located critique and an open inquiry, not a learner-interest pass.")
(.o identity: 'first-reading-bfd2c2f490f5 view: 'recovery-first-observation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-ba3dea61e60d8d456afa9d934a0cb0b9285ef6d3847fef5c60339cf29068f4ad image-sha: "bfd2c2f490f549d98aca72471135dac5833c4c02d0a6bee09527d4178568d578" question: 'what-can-we-know producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the actual first exported PNG. The title and equal fast words offer a concrete question about cause, but the picture does not yet meet the young-novice goal. The unknown file's bare question mark does not distinguish unknown content from unknown history. A torn receipt suggests a previously existing receipt was destroyed; the scenario is that no execution receipt was committed. The folder front covers Whole change and Acceptance. More importantly grouping the comparison with its terminal responsibility pushes the competing-explanation branch beyond that group: its long line runs below the folder and can be read as a mandatory sequence. Alternatives and responsibilities should remain peers of the same comparison. Text shrinks to about 14.11 px, below the unchanged reader target. Remove the misleading receipt metaphor, expose the folder questions and let the semantic branching prevent an over-wide compound group. This is an actual image critique, not a learner-understood or interest verdict.")) image-evidence: (list
